 5. 📺 Trump&#x27;s campaign ad vanishing act 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: AdImpact. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Republicans on the ballot this cycle have all but stopped mentioning President Trump in their campaign ads, according to an Axios analysis of broadcast advertising data from AdImpact.

 Why it matters: Trump has tried to make the 2026 midterms a referendum on his presidency. His party has run the other way, Axios' Sara Fischer writes. 🧮 By the numbers: Trump appeared in 66% of House Republicans' primary ads but shows up in just 3% of their general election ads.

 In Senate races, Republican ads mentioning him fell from 77% to 22%. 👓 Between the lines: This year's drop-off stands out given how hard Trump has pushed to tie himself to the midterms.

 He has urged voters to pretend he's on the ballot and essentially demanded ads running during the Republican midterm convention in September feature him. Keep reading ... Get Axios Media Trends . 

 
 
