 6. 📊 Marathon midterm count 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: AP and Edison Research via The New York Times. Chart: Andrew Pantazi/Axios Tonight's complete results might not be known for days, Axios' Andrew Pantazi writes. 

 AP didn't call control of the House until seven or eight days after Election Day in each of the past three elections. The Senate was settled at 12:06 a.m. ET on Wednesday in 2024. In 2022, it took four days, and in 2020, it wasn't called until Georgia's January runoffs, two months later. More election count stats . 

 Photo: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters Above: In closing remarks at the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool yesterday, President Trump focused more on his sweeping plans to remake Washington than on the midterms, Axios' Avery Lotz writes. 

 He praised the newly reopened pool and a new White House helipad, and laid out plans for a "triumphal arch" and a promenade from the Lincoln Memorial to the Potomac. Keep reading ... Watch the speech . 

 
 
